      'Cybersecurity: Applied Cryptography & Distributed Attacks',
      'Cybersecurity',
      'Tough theoretical questions on RSA math, Diffie-Hellman key exchange, zero-knowledge proofs, and network threat mitigation.',
      40,
      180,
      'Hard',
      'General Instructions:
1. This exam contains 60 questions across 3 sections.
2. Section A contains 25 Single Correct Option Questions. Each question has four choices, of which ONLY ONE is correct. Marks: +3 for correct, -1 for incorrect.
3. Section B contains 20 One or More Than One Correct Option(s) Questions. Marks: +4 for correct, -2 for incorrect.
4. Section C contains 15 Numerical Value Questions. The answer is a decimal or integer. Marks: +3 for correct, 0 for incorrect.
5. Total time allowed is 180 minutes. Total marks: 200.
6. The test is of extremely high, JEE-level conceptual and mathematical difficulty.',
      200,
      '[{"id":"sec_scq","name":"Section A: Single Correct Questions","description":"Questions 1-25. Marks: +3 for correct, -1 for incorrect.","positive_marks":3,"negative_marks":-1,"question_type":"single_choice"},{"id":"sec_mcq","name":"Section B: Multiple Correct Questions","description":"Questions 26-45. Marks: +4 for correct, -2 for incorrect.","positive_marks":4,"negative_marks":-2,"question_type":"multiple_choice"},{"id":"sec_nvq","name":"Section C: Numerical & Algorithmic Values","description":"Questions 46-60. Marks: +3 for correct, 0 for incorrect.","positive_marks":3,"negative_marks":0,"question_type":"numerical"}]'::jsonb,
      '[{"question":"[SCQ-1] An engineering system uses Diffie-Hellman with a baseline constraint of $\\theta = 0.15$. In the worst-case configuration, the execution is threatened by bottlenecks related to RSA Encryption. If we apply an optimization based on Zero-Knowledge Proof over a size of $N = 10$ items, which of the following is the exact boundary condition for optimal throughput?","options":["Option A: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(N \\log N)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.15$","Option B: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.18$","Option C: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(N^2)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.12$","Option D: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(\\log N)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.22$"],"correct":1,"type":"single_choice","section_id":"sec_scq","explanation":"Under Cybersecurity: Applied Cryptography & Distributed Attacks specifications, resolving RSA Encryption via Zero-Knowledge Proof bounds the growth rate. The exact limit is given by Option B because it matches the partition boundary $\\theta = 0.15."},{"question":"[SCQ-2] An engineering system uses Diffie-Hellman with a baseline constraint of $\\theta = 0.30$. In the worst-case configuration, the execution is threatened by bottlenecks related to RSA Encryption. If we apply an optimization based on Zero-Knowledge Proof over a size of $N = 20$ items, which of the following is the exact boundary condition for optimal throughput?","options":["Option A: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(N \\log N)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.30$","Option B: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.36$","Option C: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(N^2)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.24$","Option D: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(\\log N)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.45$"],"correct":2,"type":"single_choice","section_id":"sec_scq","explanation":"Under Cybersecurity: Applied Cryptography & Distributed Attacks specifications, resolving RSA Encryption via Zero-Knowledge Proof bounds the growth rate. The exact limit is given by Option C because it matches the partition boundary $\\theta = 0.30."},{"question":"[SCQ-3] An engineering system uses Diffie-Hellman with a baseline constraint of $\\theta = 0.45$. In the worst-case configuration, the execution is threatened by bottlenecks related to RSA Encryption. If we apply an optimization based on Zero-Knowledge Proof over a size of $N = 30$ items, which of the following is the exact boundary condition for optimal throughput?","options":["Option A: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(N \\log N)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.45$","Option B: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.54$","Option C: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(N^2)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.36$","Option D: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(\\log N)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.68$"],"correct":3,"type":"single_choice","section_id":"sec_scq","explanation":"Under Cybersecurity: Applied Cryptography & Distributed Attacks specifications, resolving RSA Encryption via Zero-Knowledge Proof bounds the growth rate. The exact limit is given by Option D because it matches the partition boundary $\\theta = 0.45."},{"question":"[SCQ-4] An engineering system uses Diffie-Hellman with a baseline constraint of $\\theta = 0.60$. In the worst-case configuration, the execution is threatened by bottlenecks related to RSA Encryption. If we apply an optimization based on Zero-Knowledge Proof over a size of $N = 40$ items, which of the following is the exact boundary condition for optimal throughput?","options":["Option A: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(N \\log N)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.60$","Option B: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.72$","Option C: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(N^2)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.48$","Option D: Limit $\\mathcal{O}(\\log N)$ with maximum overhead $\\approx 0.90$"],"correct":0,"type":"single_choice","section_id":"sec_scq","explanation":"Under Cybersecurity: Applied Cryptography & Distributed Attacks specifications, resolving RSA Encryption via Zero-Kn