EOQ) model, the annual demand is $D = 4600$ units, the ordering cost is $S = $50$ per order, and the holding cost is $H = $4.00$ per unit per year. Calculate the optimal order quantity (round to the nearest integer).","options":[],"correct":"339","type":"numerical","section_id":"sec_nvq","explanation":"EOQ formula is $\\sqrt{\\frac{2DS}{H}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\times 4600 \\times 50}{4}} = \\sqrt{115000} \\approx 339$."},{"question":"[NVQ-47] In an inventory management system using the Economic Order Quantity (EOQ) model, the annual demand is $D = 4700$ units, the ordering cost is $S = $50$ per order, and the holding cost is $H = $4.00$ per unit per year. Calculate the optimal order quantity (round to the nearest integer).","options":[],"correct":"343","type":"numerical","section_id":"sec_nvq","explanation":"EOQ formula is $\\sqrt{\\frac{2DS}{H}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\times 4700 \\times 50}{4}} = \\sqrt{117500} \\approx 343$."},{"question":"[NVQ-48] In an inventory management system using the Economic Order Quantity (EOQ) model, the annual demand is $D = 4800$ units, the ordering cost is $S = $50$ per order, and the holding cost is $H = $4.00$ per unit per year. Calculate the optimal order quantity (round to the nearest integer).","options":[],"correct":"346","type":"numerical","section_id":"sec_nvq","explanation":"EOQ formula is $\\sqrt{\\frac{2DS}{H}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\times 4800 \\times 50}{4}} = \\sqrt{120000} \\approx 346$."},{"question":"[NVQ-49] In an inventory management system using the Economic Order Quantity (EOQ) model, the annual demand is $D = 4900$ units, the ordering cost is $S = $50$ per order, and the holding cost is $H = $4.00$ per unit per year. Calculate the optimal order quantity (round to the nearest integer).","options":[],"correct":"350","type":"numerical","section_id":"sec_nvq","explanation":"EOQ formula is $\\sqrt{\\frac{2DS}{H}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\times 4900 \\times 50}{4}} = \\sqrt{122500} \\approx 350$."},{"question":"[NVQ-50] In an inv