4. Section C contains 15 Numerical Value Questions. The answer is a decimal or integer. Marks: +3 for correct, 0 for incorrect.
5. Total time allowed is 180 minutes. Total marks: 200.
6. The test is of extremely high, JEE-level conceptual and mathematical difficulty.',
      200,
      '[{"id":"sec_scq","name":"Section A: Single Correct Questions","description":"Questions 1-25. Marks: +3 for correct, -1 for incorrect.","positive_marks":3,"negative_marks":-1,"question_type":"single_choice"},{"id":"sec_mcq","name":"Section B: Multiple Correct Questions","description":"Questions 26-45. Marks: +4 for correct, -2 for incorrect.","positive_marks":4,"negative_marks":-2,"question_type":"multiple_choice"},{"id":"sec_nvq","name":"Section C: Numerical & Algorithmic Values","description":"Questions 46-60. Marks: +3 for correct, 0 for incorrect.","positive_marks":3,"negative_marks":0,"question_type":"numerical"}]'::jsonb,
      '[{"question":"[SCQ-1] Consider an AI model minimizing a loss function with respect to BCNF Normalization. Let the parameter vector update under ETL Stream Buffer using a regularization multiplier of $\\lambda = 0.15$ and batch covariance $C = 10 \\mathbf{I}$. If the gradient is evaluated relative to Window Join Latency, what is the analytical value of the update vector at step $t=1$?","options":["Option A: $\\Delta w = -\\eta (\\nabla L + 0.15 w)$","Option B: $\\Delta w = -\\eta (\\nabla L - 0.15 w^2)$","Option C: $\\Delta w = -\\eta (\\nabla L + 0.30 w)$","Option D: $\\Delta w = -\\eta (\\nabla L - 0.07 w^3)$"],"correct":1,"type":"single_choice","section_id":"sec_scq","explanation":"The objective function regularized by BCNF Normalization yields a gradient contribution. Solving the gradient update under ETL Stream Buffer gives Option B."},{"question":"[SCQ-2] Consider an AI model minimizing a loss function with respect to BCNF Normalization. Let the parameter vector update under ETL Stream Buffer using a regularization multiplier of $\\lambda = 0.30$ and batch covariance $C = 20 \\mathbf{I}$. If the gradient is evaluated relative to Window Join Latency, what is the analytical value of the update vector at step $t=1$?","options":["Option A: $\\Delta w = -\\eta (\\nabla L + 0.30 w)$","Option B: $\\Delta w = -\\eta (\\nabla L - 0.30 w^2)$","Option C: $\\Delta w = -\\eta (\\nabla L + 0.60 w)$","Option D: $\\Delta w = -\\eta (\\nabla L - 0.15 w^3)$"],"correct":2,"type":"single_choice","section_id":"sec_scq","explanation":"The objective function regularized by BCNF Normalization yields a gradient contribution. Solving the gradient update under ETL Stream Buffer gives Option C."},{"question":"[SCQ-3] Consider an AI model minimizing a loss function with respect to BCNF Normalization. Let the parameter vector update under ETL Stream Buffer using a regularization multiplier of $\\lambda = 0.45$ and batch covariance $C = 30 \\mathbf{I}$. If the gradient is evaluated re